[[file:Cooldown_Icon.png|20px]] '''Cooldown''' (abbreviated as CD) is an attribute of champion abilities, items, summoner spell and runes. It is the amount of time before a champion ability, item, summoner spell or rune can be used again after activation. When an ability, item, summoner spell or rune is in this state, it is considered to be "on cooldown". Cooldown is directly affected by [[ability haste]], [[ability haste#Increasing item haste|item haste]] and [[ability haste#Increasing summoner spell haste|summoner spell haste]] which will lessen the amount of time an ability, item or summoner spell, respectively, is unusable after activation.

Some abilities cannot affect targets again within a duration, a mechanic called target immunity {{sti|cooldown}} or on-target cooldown. On-target durations may or may not be affected by haste, depending on the spell.

== Cooldown champions ==
{{main|:Category:Cooldown champion|Cooldown champions}}
Similar to {{tip|Mana}}, '''Cooldown''' limits ability use. For some champions, cooldowns are the only limitation to their ability usage. These are: 

