== Ability haste ==
{{as|{{sti|'''Ability haste'''}}|ability haste}}, or {{as|{{sti|'''AH'''}}|ability haste}} reduces the cooldowns of [[champion ability|champion abilities]] by a percentage. It is the most common form of '''haste''' and it is the only '''haste''' stat that is displayed by the game client in the HUD's player stat overview. It is capped at '''500''', which is equivalent to {{fd|83.{{recurring|3}}}}% cooldown reduction.
* Ability haste itself {{tip|stacks additively}}, and each point acquired directly adds to the statistic (1:1).

'''Ability haste''' can be gained from [[Buff|buffs]], [[item]]s and [[rune]]s.

{{gold value}}
* '''Ability haste''' has a gold value of {{g|{{#invoke:Gold value|wikivaluedefine}}{{#expr:{{#var:ah}} round 2}}}} per point.
<br/>
=== Scaling with ability haste ===
It is important to note that '''any''' cooldown that can be reduced through cooldown reduction, will innately scale off of haste (which is, of course, cooldown reduction). However, certain mechanics are special-cased to be affected by ability haste whereas they normally would not be. There are currently no such effects.

