'''Healing''' is the action of replenishing a unit's current [[health]], distinct from the other forms of health restoration ([[life steal]], [[spell vamp]], [[omnivamp]] and [[health regeneration]]). It can be weakened by healing reduction.

'''Healing''' cannot increase a unit's current health over its maximum. The act of [[Experience (champion)|leveling up]] and certain [[Health#Champion abilities|champion abilities]] (such as {{cai|Wild Growth|Lulu}}) will increase a unit's current health by the same amount as the increase to their maximum health, but this is not considered a form of healing. As a result, they are not affected by healing reduction.

'''Healing''' can reduce a unit's current health if the heal value is negative (e.g. by having a negative [[stat]] scaling with it). This is not considered [[damage]] and will not trigger damage-related events; for this same reason, it also cannot [[kill]] a unit. In any case, the unit's health cannot be reduced below 0.

