== Multi-kill ==
A multi-kill is the act of killing several champions within 10 seconds<ref>Since patch [[V1.0.0.147]]</ref> of each other, with this window refreshing on scoring a kill.<ref>Since patch [[V1.0.0.85]]</ref> After scoring a Quadra Kill, the window for scoring a Pentakill increases to 30 seconds; if an enemy respawns before this time, the window ends prematurely.

Special announcements play for champions who score multi-kills: "<code><Player1> has slain <Player2> for a <Multi-kill>!</code>"

* Double Kill (2)
* Triple Kill (3)
* Quadra Kill (4)
* Pentakill (5)
* Hexakill (6), only on the {{tip|Hexakill}} mode

;Notes
* The window for a pentakill also has a minimum of 10 seconds, just like any other kill in a multi-kill sequence. This is not currently applicable in most game modes however.
* A multi-kill of six or more champions outside of {{tip|Hexakill}} mode is not announced. Even if a champion manages to kill seven champions within the time window, the seventh kill is not announced as a Double Kill. It would be accurately recorded in the "Largest Multi Kill" in the post-match stats, however. The kill sound effect of a Pentakill is played for every additional kill in the multi-kill after 5.

;History:Some footage from before the time {{tip|Hexakill}} was introduced showcases the possibility of achieving a ''Legendary Kill'', which can occur after killing another enemy after a Pentakill, on any gamemode other than '''Hexakill'''.<ref>[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uEkiKHldSvo&ab_channel=Exil Legendary Kill]</ref> However, this feature seems to have been removed from the game, and the time at which it occurred is uncertain.

== Ace ==
An '''ace''' is scored by killing the last living champion of the enemy team. Scoring an ace is far easier than scoring a Pentakill, since the only requisite is for the entire allied team to kill the enemy team, rather than one player to kill the entire enemy team. There is no direct bonus associated with an ace, but it is accompanied by a unique announcement that credits the player who scored it.

Both teams can be aced at the same time, leaving no champions alive on the map.

== Kill sound effects ==
Scoring a kill or [[assist]] on an enemy champion plays unique musical stings as a celebration. Kills specifically are accompanied by background foley. When scoring a multi-kill, the audio increases in musical intensity with each kill, also overriding the previous one each time if currently playing.

* {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Generic.ogg}} ''Kill Foley''
* {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Point First.ogg}} {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Melody First.ogg}} ''First Kill Celebration''
* {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Point Double.ogg}} {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Melody Double.ogg}} ''Double Kill Celebration''
* {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Point Triple.ogg}} {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Melody Triple.ogg}} ''Triple Kill Celebration''
* {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Point Quadra.ogg}} {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Melody Quadra.ogg}} ''Quadra Kill Celebration''
* {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Point Penta.ogg}} {{sm2|Killstreak SFX Multikill Melody Penta.ogg}} ''Pentakill Celebration''
