:''For the virtual band and associated content, see {{univ|True Damage}}.''
:''For the trait in {{tip|teamfight Tactics}}, see {{TFTt|True Damage}}.'' 
:''For the other types of damage see: [[Magic damage]] and [[Physical damage]].''

'''{{as|True damage}}''' is one of the three types of [[damage]] in [[League of Legends]] and is the least common form of damage. True damage is dealt by some [[champion ability|abilities]], [[item]]s, [[rune]]s, [[buff]]s, and [[summoner spell]]s.

Unless otherwise stated, true damage ignores [[Damage_modifier#Decreasing_damage_received|damage reduction]] (e.g. {{stil|{{as|armor}}}} and {{stil|{{as|magic resistance}}}}, {{ai|Unbreakable Will|Alistar}}, {{si|Exhaust}}).

As of patch [[V25.S1.3]], true damage '''is affected by all [[Damage modifier#Items|damage amplifiers]]''' with the exception of {{cai|Hemoplague|Vladimir}}{{bug}}. True damage dealt by Jungle items ({{ii|Gustwalker Hatchling|icononly=true}}{{ii|Mosstomper Seedling|icononly=true}}{{ii|Scorchclaw Pup|icononly=true}}), {{si|Smite}} (including its upgrades), and {{si|Ignite}} cannot be amplified under any circumstance.

== Blocking true damage ==
* [[Champion ability|Abilities]] or [[summoner spell]]s which deal true damage are still blocked by {{tip|spell shield}}, unless otherwise noted.
* [[Attack_effects#Parrying|Parries]] can block the true damage from [[basic attack]]s and {{tip|on-hit}} effects.
* {{tip|Invulnerability}} will block all types of damage ''including'' true damage.

== Countering true damage ==
'''True damage''' cannot be mitigated or reduced, but there are ways to counter it:
* Stacking {{sti|health|link=true}} causes sources of flat true damage (e.g. {{si|Ignite}}) to effectively deal a lesser percentage of total health.
* Normal {{tip|Shield|shields}} can absorb true damage at any amount.

