: {{Hatnote|''For other games and uses of "unit", see [[Unit (disambiguation)]].''}}
A '''unit''' in {{tip|League of Legends}} is an entity that possesses [[sight]], [[statistics]], and any number of [[Terminology#Spell|spells]]. The most notable statistic is [[health|health points]]—of which all units have at least 1—and the most notable spell is the [[basic attack]]. Units can also have [[buff]]s and [[debuff]]s applied to them.

The following types of '''units''' exist. Any interactions between them are either inherent or result from spells.
* [[Structure]] ({{tip|Turret}}, [[Inhibitor]], [[Nexus]])
* {{tip|Champion}}
* {{tip|Minion}}
* {{tip|Monster}}
* {{tip|Ward}}
* [[Champion summoned units|Summon]] ([[Terrain#Player-Generated|champion-generated terrain]] and {{tip|pets}})
* [[Jungle plants|Jungle plant]]

A unit can be allied, enemied, or neutral in relation to another unit. ''Neutral'' units are those who only act as enemies when aggression has been initiated against them. The relation of units is relevant for NPC and player target acquisition and gameplay interaction.

